Affinity - Affinity tells to Kubernetes whree to place a pod in cluster. It helps to control where pods are schedule based on rule.
There are mainly three types of Affinity:
1. Node Affinity- Node Affinity tells to pod "only run to a certain nodes". It used when you want a pods on specific Hardware or environments.
2. Pod Affinity- Pod Affinity tell to kubernetes "place a pod close to other pods".
 ex.- run backend pods near fronted pods. 
3. Pod Anti Affinity- It tells to kubernetes "don't place this pods near to other pods."
 ex.- don't put two replicas on a same node.

